              KNN Algorithm

For a new flower, the program calculates the Euclidean distance between the new flower and every training flower.

The formula is:

Distance = √((x1-y1)² + (x2-y2)² + (x3-y3)² + (x4-y4)²)

The program selects the closest K = 3 flowers.

The species receiving the most votes becomes the prediction